<header><p class="st-kicker">electorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Electorate of Mainz</h1><p class="st-meta">780 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Mainz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The most powerful church state of the Holy Roman Empire, whose archbishop was arch-chancellor of Germany and convened the elections of kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The see of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> was raised to an archbishopric around 780 to 782, building on the work of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a>, archbishop there from 746. Its province became the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Christendom</a>. Royal grants from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottonian-dynasty">Ottonians</a> onwards gave the archbishops temporal lordship over Mainz and scattered lands along the Main, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eichsfeld">Eichsfeld</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From 965 the archbishop held the title of arch-chancellor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> confirmed him as first among the seven prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, presiding over imperial elections. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> was governed by its cathedral chapter and archbishop. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Gutenberg</a> invented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> there in the 1450s, and the university was founded in 1477.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">Revolutionary Wars</a>, and the short-lived <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-mainz">Republic of Mainz</a> was proclaimed in 1793. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichsdeputationshauptschluss">Reichsdeputationshauptschluss</a> of 1803 dissolved the electorate; its last elector, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-theodor-von-dalberg">Karl Theodor von Dalberg</a>, kept a state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschaffenburg">Aschaffenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-regensburg">Regensburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/electorate-of-mainz.jpg" alt="Electorate of Mainz" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan, wheel from File:Coat of Arms of Ernest August, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1661-1692).svg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Electorate_of_Mainz.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>780 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>electorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mainz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Willigis, Albert of Brandenburg, Karl Theodor von Dalberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Archbishopric of Mainz, Kurmainz, Electoral Mainz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1292&amp;focus=electorate-of-mainz" aria-label="Electorate of Mainz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4870 438 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Electorate of Mainz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5190 694L5139 672M5190 694L5199 691M5190 694L5229 694M5190 694L5279 723M5190 694L5197 704M5190 694L5190 694"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5199 691h0M5229 694h0M5279 723h0M5197 704h0M5190 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" 